# Initial-round experiment and attempt record

This is the baseline implementation round. No optimization lane was run; zero optimization hypotheses have been consumed. In particular, group commit was not implemented. No measurements here support a language-performance comparison.

Baseline design hypothesis: serial ownership of durable state can give cancellation and terminal writes a legal ordering while four independent workers retain native concurrency. Socket/crash and Go race tests support the exercised histories; they do not prove all possible interleavings.

