## Scope of evidence

The independent inspector is candidate-owned Python using only the standard library and dynamic RocksDB C API; it does not use service status as its oracle. It opens only after the writer has exited. Crash tests check complete old/new logical state, retained acknowledged payloads, receipts, id bijection, contiguous checkpoint, pending accounting and cancellation persistence. No external evaluator, other workspace, repository, network, Bitcoin library or other agent was accessed.

No native diagnostic instrumentation was supplied or constructed. Go race checks cover exercised Go paths, not native library races. The test suite does not deterministically hold C call-entry/write barriers, inject storage/allocation failures, prove admission-limit saturation, or simulate power loss. The native adapter and durability settings were unchanged.

